<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  THE GAMMA ZONE CORPUS ARCHIVE, on the DEV Mac, hourly.

  oe-archive-gamma-zone.sh runs oe-archive-kafka.sh with ENV=dev and TOPICS="$GAMMA_ZONE_CORPUS"
  (oe-topics.env: options.spx.gamma-zone.log) against the dev broker, and writes gzipped JSON Lines
  to LOCAL DISK on this host.

  WHY HERE AND NOT ON .252. The .252 crontab's archive entries are disabled by the owner with the
  reason written beside them — "archive moves to dev" — and this is that move for this topic.
  Running on the dev Mac also removes a failure path: from the 201 Mac the dev broker is reachable
  only through an SSH tunnel on 127.0.0.1:19092 whose launchd job has exited 255 before, and the
  broker advertises host.docker.internal, which resolves to 127.0.0.1 on any Mac running Docker
  Desktop. On THIS host localhost:19092 reaches the real broker with nothing in between.

  WHY HOURLY. The archiver is incremental and offset-checkpointed, so a no-op run costs nothing and
  a run that finds one new emission writes one small file. The topic is excluded from all four dev
  deletion paths by name — but that is the protection that failed before, when a cleanup run
  destroyed ten keep-list topics it had just printed as kept. An hour is the most this can lose.

  LOCAL DISK, NOT THE NAS (owner, 2026-11-11). ARCHIVE_DIR is deliberately NOT set here: the wrapper
  defaults it to $HOME/oe-ops/gamma-zone-corpus and passes ALLOW_NON_NAS itself. Unlike
  oe-archive-depth.plist beside it, this job does NOT want the NAS sentinel — the NAS is at 100%
  (906G of 906G) and nothing has archived anywhere since 2026-10-26, so a NAS destination would be
  an hourly failure. Set ARCHIVE_DIR here only to move the destination, and move the existing tree
  with it: the offsets checkpoint lives under ARCHIVE_DIR, so a fresh directory re-archives from
  offset 0 and duplicates everything already captured.

  THE SCHEDULE IS THE HOST'S LOCAL CLOCK. launchd has no CRON_TZ; StartCalendarInterval with only a
  Minute fires at minute 0 of every LOCAL hour. It stays hourly through a daylight-saving switch and
  through a change of the host's timezone; what moves is which UTC instant each run lands on, and
  nothing here depends on that. An earlier draft of this comment claimed the runs were "the same
  instant in any zone", which is simply false. The checkpoint, not the schedule, decides what a run
  reads.

  Install: run scripts/ops/archive/install-dev-mac-gamma-zone-archive.sh ON THIS HOST. Do not copy
  files by hand. Unlike the depth archive this job needs NO canonical-archive helper jar and no
  contracts jar — options.spx.gamma-zone.log is JSON on the wire and takes the plain console path.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.optionsedge.oe-archive-gamma-zone</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/abhinav/oe-ops/oe-archive-gamma-zone.sh</string>
  </array>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key><string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/abhinav/oe-ops/archive-gamma-zone.launchd.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/abhinav/oe-ops/archive-gamma-zone.launchd.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
